/ Captured sessions: the connections in the window that ended abnormally
/ while trace capture was on, so they have a stored transcript
/ (SessionTranscript). The history table below links to these too, but
/ only one row in dozens carries one; this table is just the ones worth
/ reading, with the peer's opening commands inline so a run of probes
/ can be triaged without opening each capture.
- setting = "#{controller_name}_trace_capture"
section.mt-4.rounded-lg.border.border-slate-200.dark:border-slate-800.bg-white.dark:bg-slate-900
  header.border-b.border-slate-200.dark:border-slate-800.px-4.py-3
    h2.font-semibold Captured sessions
    p.text-sm.text-slate-500.dark:text-slate-400
      ' Connections in the selected window whose dialogue was captured
      ' because they ended abnormally - timeouts, drops, protocol errors,
      ' failed logins - while the #{setting} setting was on. Newest first,
      ' kept #{MailOnRails::SessionTranscript.retention_days} days.
      - unless @capture_on
        span.ml-1.font-medium.text-amber-700.dark:text-amber-400
          = "#{setting} is off, so nothing new is being captured."
  - if @transcripts.any?
    table.w-full.text-sm
      thead.text-left.text-xs.text-slate-500.dark:text-slate-400
        tr
          th.px-4.py-2 Closed
          th.px-4.py-2 Address
          th.px-4.py-2 Listener
          th.px-4.py-2 User
          th.px-4.py-2 Reason
          th.px-4.py-2.text-right Lines
          th.px-4.py-2 Peer sent
          th.px-4.py-2
      tbody
        - @transcripts.each do |capture|
          tr.border-t.border-slate-100.dark:border-slate-800
            td.px-4.py-1.5.whitespace-nowrap.text-slate-600.dark:text-slate-300
              = link_to capture.closed_at.strftime("%b %-d %H:%M"), session_transcript_path(capture), class: "hover:text-accent hover:underline"
            td.px-4.py-1.5.font-mono.break-all
              = capture.ip || "?"
              = render "ip_meta", ip: capture.ip
            td.px-4.py-1.5.text-slate-600.dark:text-slate-300= capture.port || "-"
            td.px-4.py-1.5.font-mono.break-all= capture.username || "-"
            td.px-4.py-1.5.text-slate-600.dark:text-slate-300= capture.close_reason&.tr("_", " ") || "-"
            td.px-4.py-1.5.text-right.tabular-nums.text-slate-600.dark:text-slate-300= capture.line_count
            td.px-4.py-1.5.font-mono.text-xs.break-all.text-slate-600.dark:text-slate-300 title="First commands the peer sent; open the transcript for the full exchange."
              = capture.preview.presence || "-"
            td.px-4.py-1.5.whitespace-nowrap.text-right
              = link_to "Transcript", session_transcript_path(capture), class: "mr-2 text-xs font-medium text-accent hover:underline"
              - if capture.ip
                = render "auth_attempts/ban_button", target: capture.ip, origin: controller_name, confirm: "Ban #{capture.ip}? Its live connections are dropped and it loses SMTP, IMAP and web login access."
  - else
    p.px-4.py-3.text-sm.text-slate-500.dark:text-slate-400 Nothing captured in this window.
